ach retry."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The provided transformation closure is executed ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" each retry, allowing for side effects such as refreshing tokens or resetting state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The closure’s returned ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always fully consumed before the retry occurs, but its elements are ignored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The element type of the returned sequence does not need to match the upstream’s element type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for performing asynchronous side effects like credential refresh before retrying the main sequence."}]},{"anchor":"Example-Refreshing-an-access-token-on-a-401-HTTP-error-before-retrying-the-main-request","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example: Refreshing an access token on a 401 HTTP error before retrying the main request"},{"code":["let mainRequest = URLSession.shared.dataTaskAsyncSequence(for: URLRequest(url: URL(string: \"https:\/\/api.example.com\/data\")!))","","let retriedSequence = mainRequest.retry(.byCount(3)) { error in","    \/\/ If error is 401 Unauthorized, refresh token before retrying","    DeferredTask {","        if let urlError = error as? URLError, urlError.code == .userAuthenticationRequired {","            try await refreshAccessToken()","        }","    }","    .toAsyncSequence() \/\/ This sequence is fully consumed before retrying, ignoring its elements","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"retry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"D","kind